caption: Path expression grammar
tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/reference
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/reference/path-grammar
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

```
path     := segment ( separator segment )*
segment  := key | "[" ( index | "*" ) "]" | "[" quoted "]"
key      := [^.[\]/]+                      (one or more non-reserved chars)
quoted   := '"' ( [^"\\] | '\\"' | '\\\\' )* '"'   (any key at all, escaped)
index    := [0-9]+
separator:= "." | (no separator before "[")
prefix   := ( ".." "/" )*                  (only in binding tokens)
```

''Quoted segments.''  A key the bare syntax cannot express — one
containing `.`, `[`, `]` or `/`, an empty one, or one starting with `@`
(reserved for context paths) — is written in double quotes inside
brackets, with no dot before it: `["first.last"].x`, `data["odd key"][*]`,
`["@id"]`.  Inside the quotes `\"` and `\\` are the only escapes.  The
pickers emit this form automatically for such keys.
